       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose. Some patients start at 2.5 mg.\n- **Amlodipine 20 mg**, if you intend it. For example, you might be working from a specialist recommendation. If so, please confirm. I'll enter it with a note documenting that the dose is above the usual maximum.\n\nIf blood pressure is still uncontrolled on 10 mg, adding a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic, is generally preferred to going higher.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
